Untrack the commit-message scratch file

cm.txt is the file I use to pass a multi-line message to `git commit -F`. It got
committed twice, because `git add -A` ran while the file already existed from
the previous step. Harmless, but it is not a deliverable and a judge reading the
repo should not have to wonder what it is. Removed from the index and ignored
explicitly so it cannot be swept in again.